# Course Slide Content Rules

## Product shape
- Professional lecture notes: bilingual EN + ZH, Windows-first
- Prefer explanation paragraphs (`bodyEn`/`bodyZh`) and clear structure
- Course photos are currently unused — do not add `image` / `images` fields unless the user explicitly asks

## Data model
- Chapters: `frontend/src/data/chapters/ch-{part}-{slug}.ts`
- Slide ids: `{file-stem}-{slug}`
- Register in `frontend/src/data/chapters/index.ts` and `parts.ts`
- Follow `frontend/src/types/course.ts`
- From `frontend/`: `npm run check:course`

## Layouts
- `title`: chapter opener
- `text`: full-width explanation (default for most concept slides)
- `split`: reserved for future text + media if images return
- `steps`: numbered Windows try-it procedures
- `callout`: goals, common mistakes, check-yourself

## Writing
- Prefer explanation over decoration: fuller `bodyEn`/`bodyZh` on concept slides when useful
- Bullets are optional support; do not default to exactly 3. Use 0, 2, 4, 5, or 6+ as the idea needs
- Keywords `{ en, zh }` on important terms
- Windows-first: PowerShell, File Explorer, `py`, `C:\` paths
- No comments in TypeScript source
